-- title:
--   Each branch ideal at a crossing is generated by two elements
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ with $5 \le p$ and a package $\mathfrak X$ of type `DRModelPackage p`, the bundled data asserting that `DRModel.toBase p` is proper and flat, that `DRModel p` is integral with integrally closed sections on affine opens, together with curve models of the modular function field over $\mathbb Q$ and over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with their Galois and place compatibilities, the two sections `εinf`, `εzero`, a distinguished smooth locus, and the further data of that structure. Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is the ideal generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Let $n$ be a point of the scheme $\mathrm{pullback}(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa, \mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa)$, and write $x_n = \mathfrak X.\mathrm{crossingPt}\,O\,\kappa\,\mathrm{to}\kappa\,n$ for its image in $X_O := \mathrm{pullback}(\mathtt{DRModel.toBase}\ p, \operatorname{Spec}(\mathbb Z \to O))$ under $\mathrm{pullback.fst}$ followed by $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ followed by the base-change map along $\mathrm{to}\kappa$. Assume the two points $\mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{inf}$ and $\mathfrak X.\xi\mathrm{zero}$ (formed from $O$, $\kappa$, $\mathrm{to}\kappa$) each specialise to $x_n$, giving branch ideals $P_\infty, P_0 \subseteq \mathcal O_{X_O, x_n}$, the preimages of the maximal ideals of the stalks at $\xi_\infty$, $\xi_0$ under the respective stalk specialisation maps. Let $\varpi_x$ denote `baseGerm`, the germ at $x_n$ of the global section of $X_O$ obtained from $p \in O$ via the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} O$. Then there is $a$ in the stalk with $(a, \varpi_x) = P_\infty$, and there is $b$ in the stalk with $(b, \varpi_x) = P_0$.
--
--   This records the local shape of the Deligne–Rapoport model at an ordinary double point of its fibre over $p$: each of the two branch ideals at a crossing needs only one generator beyond the uniformiser of the base. It feeds the construction of oriented crossing charts in [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.forall_exists_orientedCrossingChart).
